WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
Most video players put the words at the bottom and the controls on top of them.

00:03.200 --> 00:06.400
Verbatim flips that. The sentence you are hearing is the control bar.

00:06.400 --> 00:09.600
Each word fills in as it is spoken, so you can see exactly where you are.

00:09.600 --> 00:12.800
Drag along the words to scrub. Click any word to jump straight to it.

00:12.800 --> 00:16.000
Paragraph breaks become chapters, and a thin track underneath keeps seeking visible.

00:16.000 --> 00:20.000
It is built for video podcasts, lectures, archives, and portfolios like this one.

00:20.000 --> 00:24.000
On a dark frame the plate stays legible, because colour is translucent, not the text.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
On a phone the sentence steps aside and a normal seek bar takes over.

00:28.000 --> 00:32.000
Every control is reachable by keyboard, and focus is always visible.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
When reduced motion is on, the words stop animating and simply switch.

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
That is Verbatim: a player you can read.
